{"path":"std/macro.format.html","title":"Macro format","description":"Creates a String using interpolation of runtime expressions.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Macro format"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/alloc/macros.rs.html#111","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"macro_rules! format {\n    ($($arg:tt)*) => { ... };\n}"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"String"},{"type":"text","value":" using interpolation of runtime expressions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first argument "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format!"},{"type":"text","value":" receives is a format string. This must be a string literal. The power of the formatting string is in the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"s contained. Additional parameters passed to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format!"},{"type":"text","value":" replace the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"{}"},{"type":"text","value":"s within the formatting string in the order given unless named or positional parameters are used."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fmt/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"the formatting syntax documentation in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"std::fmt"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for details."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A common use for "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"format!"},{"type":"text","value":" is concatenation and interpolation of strings. The same convention is used with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.print.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"print!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.write.html","title":"macro std::write","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"write!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" macros, depending on the intended destination of the string; all these macros internally use "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.format_args.html","title":"macro std::format_args","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"format_args!"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To convert a single value to a string, use the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/string/trait.ToString.html","title":"trait std::string::ToString","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"to_string"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method. This will use the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fmt/trait.Display.html","title":"trait std::fmt::Display","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Display"}]},{"type":"text","value":" formatting trait."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To concatenate literals into a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"&'static str"},{"type":"text","value":", use the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.concat.html","title":"macro std::concat","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"concat!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" macro."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"panics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Panics"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"format!"},{"type":"text","value":" panics if a formatting trait implementation returns an error. This indicates an incorrect implementation since "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"fmt::Write for String"},{"type":"text","value":" never returns an error itself."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"format!(\"test\");                             // => \"test\"\nformat!(\"hello {}\", \"world!\");               // => \"hello world!\"\nformat!(\"x = {}, y = {val}\", 10, val = 30);  // => \"x = 10, y = 30\"\nlet (x, y) = (1, 2);\nformat!(\"{x} + {y} = 3\");                    // => \"1 + 2 = 3\""},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0A%23!%5Ballow(unused_must_use)%5D%0A%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++format!(%22test%22);+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++//+=%3E+%22test%22%0A++++format!(%22hello+%7B%7D%22,+%22world!%22);+++++++++++++++//+=%3E+%22hello+world!%22%0A++++format!(%22x+=+%7B%7D,+y+=+%7Bval%7D%22,+10,+val+=+30);++//+=%3E+%22x+=+10,+y+=+30%22%0A++++let+(x,+y)+=+(1,+2);%0A++++format!(%22%7Bx%7D+%2B+%7By%7D+=+3%22);%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]}]}}
